<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ly Phat Tu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 571–602</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Lý Phật Tử</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ly Phat Tu was the last ruler of the Early Ly dynasty in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, holding power from 571 to 602. He took the throne from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trieu-quang-phuc">Trieu Quang Phuc</a> and held the Red River delta through a mix of warfare and negotiation. In 602 he surrendered to a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui</a> army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-fang">Liu Fang</a>, ending the dynasty, and was taken to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</p></div>
